  "query_preview": "..Been a busy solo morning with showers and isolated\nthunderstorms moving across eastern Pinal, eastern Pima, southern\nGraham and northwest Cochise county. Some of the heavier \nshowers have had some impresssive rainfall rates, up to 2\"/hr, \nwhich resulted a few small stream advisories and a flash flood \nwarning being issued. Some washes across the above mentioned \nareas have seen some good responses to the rainfall. All of this\nis associated with an upper level trof to our west that extended\nfrom wrn NV to srn CA. These showers/storms will continue to move\nto the east-northeast this morning and gradually decrease in \nareal coverage as the morning progresses. Satellite imagery this\nmorning showed clearer skies across southwest Arizona. So expect\npartly cloudy skies once the showers end and then see scattered\nredevelopment of low-topped showers/storms with the afternoon \nheating and the dynamics associated with the above mentioned \ntrof. Can't rule out a frisky storm or two producing very small\nhail with the cool summer mid-level 500 mb temps of -6C.\n\nDrier does filters in across the area tomorrow and continuing\ninto this weekend. Still enough moisture around for a chance of\nafternoon/evening storms mainly south and east of Tucson. The\nonce caveat to this is the potential for an easterly wave, which\nis currently along the Mexican coast of the GoA, moving across \nnorthern Mexico on Sunday. Something to keep an eye one as this\nmay bring a better chance of storms that what is currently in\nthe forecast.\n\nTemperatures will be below normal today, then warm up again to \nabove normal this weekend into next week with moderate to\nlocalized Major HeatRisk and triple digit highs returning to\nmost of the area.",
